        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(plugins): add Computer Use provider contract",
        "body": "Closes #97938\n\nRelated: #97939\n\nSupersedes #101564 without closing it. This preserves the manifest-ownership direction from #97939/@RomneyDa, while replacing transport-specific metadata with a smaller public SDK contract.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nComputer Use plugins need a stable way to declare provider ownership before plugin runtime loads, and Wave 2 node-host work needs a provider identity it can consume without core hardcoding a bundled implementation. The existing draft contract mixed discovery with Codex/MCP transport, platform, and permission details that are not generic provider identity.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds `contracts.computerUseProviders` for static ownership and `api.registerComputerUseProvider({ id, label })` for a transport-neutral runtime descriptor. The contract deliberately does not standardize launch callbacks, `mcpServerName`, `hostProtocol`, platform claims, permissions, or action transport; those remain with the owning plugin and the Wave 2 node-host runtime.\n\nManifest ownership is discovery metadata, not authorization to use Accessibility, Screen Recording, or other host permissions.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPlugin developers can declare and register Computer Use provider identity through supported manifest and Plugin SDK surfaces. Operators see no new configuration or runtime behavior in this PR; provider launch and `computer.act` fulfillment remain follow-up runtime work.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused manifest, registry, transaction rollback, captured-registration, packed public-SDK fixture, and API-baseline tests: 207 tests passed across five Vitest shards using `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs`.\n- Plugin SDK API baseline, package export, and 8,154-export surface budget checks passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `pnpm check:changed` passed the scoped core/extensions/scripts/docs/tooling lanes, including all required typecheck, lint, boundary, import-cycle, and policy gates.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `pnpm build` passed, including the published Plugin SDK declaration graph and export verification.\n- Two fresh uncommitted Codex autoreviews reported no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Direct upstream Codex inspection confirmed Computer Use is currently a discoverable plugin with MCP configuration, not a generic host provider protocol; this is why MCP server naming is outside this contract.\n\nAI-assisted: implementation and validation were completed with Codex; the final diff and dependency contract were reviewed directly.\n",
